From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anxelok <anxelok@localhost>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 10:48:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Trim always-on overhead from the hot tick paths

Profiling with all patches read end to end found a diffuse tax rather
than one hot spot; this takes the mechanical parts:

Ownership-check, dispatch and drain counters were shared AtomicLongs
bumped from every region thread (the ownership counter on every check,
the dispatch pair on every owner-domain execute), which ping-pongs the
cache line across workers. They are LongAdders now.

The relaxed block-state read fetched the already-loaded chunk, then
returned null so the normal path fetched it a second time, with an
ownership walk in between. A loaded chunk now answers directly: reads
are identical for owner and off-owner while mutations are staged, so
the ownership walk only runs for unloaded chunks.

The per-domain random sources are thread-confined, so they use the
non-atomic SingleThreadedRandomSource; the sequence is identical to
LegacyRandomSource, without a compare-and-set per sample.

Staged-event veto bookkeeping is allocated lazily; the common phase
with no cancelled events no longer allocates the veto sets.

